@startuml
title Generic Grid<T> / VirtualGrid<T> (proposed templated redesign)

class "Range" as Range {
  +begin: uint16_t
  +end: uint16_t
  +contains(idx): bool
  +size(): uint16_t
}
note top of Range
  Not templated -- pure index
  math, no dependency on T.
end note

interface "Device<T>" as Device {
  +operator[](index): T&
  +count(): uint16_t
}
note right of Device
  Replaces LEDStrip.
  Any 1D indexable backing
  store: LED strip, DMX
  channel array, servo bank,
  std::vector<T> for tests...
end note

class "DeviceMapping<T>" as DeviceMapping {
  +device: Device<T>*
  +xRange: Range
  +yRange: Range
  +contains(x, y): bool
  +localIndex(x, y): uint16_t
}

class "Grid<T>" as Grid {
  -m_xSize: uint16_t
  -m_ySize: uint16_t
  -m_cells: vector<T*>
  +Grid(xSize, ySize)
  +addDevice(device, xRange, yRange)
  +isComplete(): bool
  +set(x, y, value: T)
  +at(x, y): T*
  -toIdx(x, y): uint16_t
}

class "VirtualGrid<T>" as VirtualGrid {
  -m_base: Grid<T>&
  -m_cfg: Config
  +VirtualGrid(base, cfg)
  +set(x, y, value: T)
}

class "VirtualGrid<T>::Config" as VGConfig {
  +xRange: Range
  +xStride: uint16_t
  +yRange: Range
  +yStride: uint16_t
}

DeviceMapping "1" o-- "2" Range : xRange / yRange
DeviceMapping --> Device : device *
DeviceMapping ..> Grid : used BY addDevice()\n(single source of index math)

Grid "1" o-- "many" Device : addDevice() wires\nm_cells[i] -> &device[localIndex]
Grid *-- "xSize*ySize" "T" : m_cells entries point\ninto device buffers (no copy)

VirtualGrid "1" o-- "1" Grid : m_base (reference)
VirtualGrid *-- VGConfig : m_cfg
VGConfig o-- "2" Range : xRange / yRange

note right of Grid
  m_cells[x * ySize + y] = T*
  points directly into a T
  inside some Device<T>'s buffer.
  set() writes through the
  pointer -- no copy, no flush.

  addDevice() now uses
  DeviceMapping::localIndex()
  as the single formula for
  grid-coord -> device-index,
  fixing the original flat-
  counter bug.
end note

note right of VirtualGrid
  set(x, y, value) fans out to
  base.set(xRange.begin + x*xStride + i,
            yRange.begin + y*yStride + j,
            value)
  for i in [0,xStride), j in [0,yStride)
  -- correctly covers a contiguous
  block per virtual cell (fixes the
  original x*i / y*j bug).
end note

@enduml
